Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• posts_questions.id : join key; each question’s identifier  
• posts_questions.creation_date : when the question was asked; used to get day‑of‑week and to measure the time gap to the first answer  
• posts_answers.parent_id : foreign‑key that points to the parent question; lets us match answers to their questions  
• posts_answers.creation_date : answer timestamp; we will look for the earliest one per question  
• posts_questions.answer_count : optional filter ( >0 ) to avoid joining against questions that have no answers  
• posts_questions.post_type_id : (= 1 for questions, but this table is questions‑only, so normally not needed)  
• posts_answers.post_type_id : (= 2 for answers, not needed once we already query the answer table)  

Typical conditions we may use  

• WHERE answer_count > 0              -- keep only questions that actually got answers  
• WHERE parent_id IS NOT NULL         -- only proper answers  
• TIMESTAMP_DIFF(first_answer_ts , question_ts , MINUTE) <= 60   -- answered within an hour  
• EXTRACT(DAYOFWEEK FROM question_ts) AS dow   -- day of week (1=Sunday … 7=Saturday in BigQuery)  

Ten exploratory SQL snippets (each limited to 20 rows)  

```sql
-- 1. Peek at questions: id and creation date
SELECT id, creation_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect answers: parent_id (question) and creation date
SELECT parent_id, creation_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
WHERE parent_id IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. How many answers belong to each of the first 20 questions?
SELECT q.id AS question_id,
       COUNT(a.id) AS answer_cnt
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
LEFT JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers` AS a
       ON a.parent_id = q.id
GROUP BY question_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Earliest answer timestamp per question (sample 20)
SELECT parent_id AS question_id,
       MIN(creation_date) AS first_answer_ts
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
GROUP BY question_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Gap (in minutes) between a question and its first answer (sample 20)
SELECT q.id AS question_id,
       q.creation_date AS question_ts,
       f.first_answer_ts,
       TIMESTAMP_DIFF(f.first_answer_ts, q.creation_date, MINUTE) AS minutes_to_answer
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
JOIN (
     SELECT parent_id, MIN(creation_date) AS first_answer_ts
     FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
     GROUP BY parent_id
) AS f
ON f.parent_id = q.id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Identify questions answered within 60 minutes (boolean flag, sample 20)
SELECT q.id,
       TIMESTAMP_DIFF(f.first_answer_ts, q.creation_date, MINUTE) AS minutes_to_answer,
       TIMESTAMP_DIFF(f.first_answer_ts, q.creation_date, MINUTE) <= 60 AS answered_within_hour
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
JOIN (
     SELECT parent_id, MIN(creation_date) AS first_answer_ts
     FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
     GROUP BY parent_id
) AS f
ON f.parent_id = q.id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Add day‑of‑week for each question (sample 20)
SELECT q.id,
       EXTRACT(DAYOFWEEK FROM q.creation_date) AS dow,
       TIMESTAMP_DIFF(f.first_answer_ts, q.creation_date, MINUTE) AS minutes_to_answer
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
JOIN (
     SELECT parent_id, MIN(creation_date) AS first_answer_ts
     FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
     GROUP BY parent_id
) AS f
ON f.parent_id = q.id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Percentage of questions answered within 1 hour per day of week (quick view)
SELECT
  EXTRACT(DAYOFWEEK FROM q.creation_date) AS dow,
  COUNTIF(TIMESTAMP_DIFF(f.first_answer_ts, q.creation_date, MINUTE) <= 60) AS answered_in_hour,
  COUNT(*) AS total_questions,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(TIMESTAMP_DIFF(f.first_answer_ts, q.creation_date, MINUTE) <= 60),
              COUNT(*)) AS pct_within_hour
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
JOIN (
     SELECT parent_id, MIN(creation_date) AS first_answer_ts
     FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
     GROUP BY parent_id
) AS f
ON f.parent_id = q.id
GROUP BY dow
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Rank days by percentage answered within an hour
SELECT *
FROM (
  SELECT
    EXTRACT(DAYOFWEEK FROM q.creation_date) AS dow,
    SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(TIMESTAMP_DIFF(f.first_answer_ts, q.creation_date, MINUTE) <= 60),
                COUNT(*)) AS pct_within_hour
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
  JOIN (
       SELECT parent_id, MIN(creation_date) AS first_answer_ts
       FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
       GROUP BY parent_id
  ) AS f ON f.parent_id = q.id
  GROUP BY dow
)
ORDER BY pct_within_hour DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Day of week with the third‑highest “answered in ≤1 hour” percentage
SELECT dow, pct_within_hour
FROM (
  SELECT
    EXTRACT(DAYOFWEEK FROM q.creation_date) AS dow,
    SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(TIMESTAMP_DIFF(f.first_answer_ts, q.creation_date, MINUTE) <= 60),
                COUNT(*)) AS pct_within_hour,
    DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(TIMESTAMP_DIFF(f.first_answer_ts, q.creation_date, MINUTE) <= 60),
                                            COUNT(*)) DESC) AS rnk
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
  JOIN (
       SELECT parent_id, MIN(creation_date) AS first_answer_ts
       FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
       GROUP BY parent_id
  ) AS f ON f.parent_id = q.id
  GROUP BY dow
)
WHERE rnk = 3
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query is restricted with `LIMIT 20` so you can iteratively inspect intermediate results before running a full, unrestricted version to obtain the definitive third‑highest percentage.
